<section id="video">
  <section>
    <h1>Audio &amp; video</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Text alternative</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If only sound: transcript</li>
      <li>If only images: transcript or audio track</li>
      <li>
        Video with sound and images:
        <ul>
          <li>Captions</li>
          <li>Audiodescription, if needed</li>
          <li>
            Useful but not mandatory for WCAG level AA: transcript and sign
            language
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Transcript</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>All the spoken text</li>
      <li>Who is speaking</li>
      <li>Other important sounds</li>
      <li>Audible emotions</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Transcript - good examples</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://ebuaccesscast.libsyn.com/ebuaccesscast26-transcript">
          Transcript of podcast
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.seksueelgeweld.be/#text-toggle">
          video with transcript just under video (with toggle link)
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://lv.vlaanderen.be/nl/voorlichting-info/videozone#">
          Video with transcript on separate page
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Captions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>For people with hearing impairments</li>
      <li>Include dialogs and other sound information</li>
      <li>
        Can be embedded in video (open captions) or provided in separate file
        (closed captions)
      </li>
      <li>Also very useful for non native speakers</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Captions</h2>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/video/sous_titres_abbaye.png"
      alt="YouTube video about abbaye de Villers, with captions"
    />
    <p>
      YouTube automatic captions make this easier but are not sufficient, see{' '}
      <a
        href="http://anysurfer.be/fr/blog/detail/sous-titrer-facilement-avec-laide-de-youtube"
        lang="fr">
        Sous-titrer facilement à l'aide de YouTube
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="present" style="top: -229px; display: block;">
    <h2>Audiodescription</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>WCAG level AA</li>
      <li>Audio track for people who are visually impaired</li>
      <li>Describes important visual information</li>
      <li>
        Examples:
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a
              lang="fr"
              href="https://audiodescriptionfrance.wordpress.com/extraits/">
              Extraits sur le site de l'AFA
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://youtu.be/rgRv4bSdLdU?list=PL4wpa1QsAPiJfQC2xA_InY02LpFufintz"
              target="_blank">
              The Interviewer
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="present" style="top: -229px; display: block;">
    <h2>Audiodescription can be avoided</h2>
    <blockquote>Call us at this number</blockquote>
  </section>
  <section>
    <blockquote>
      On this graph you can see the evolution of number of patients admitted
      last week at the hospital.
    </blockquote>
  </section>
  <section>
    <blockquote>
      The number of patients admitted last week in the hospital decreased from
      100 on monday to 50 on sunday.
    </blockquote>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Sound should not start automatically</h2>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use an accessible media player</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Flash players and native HTML5 player are not good enough</li>
      <li>Use a player with accessible controls</li>
      <li>Foresee support for captions</li>
      <li>
        Good examples:
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="http://ableplayer.github.io/ableplayer/tests/test3.html">
              Able player
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/Selz/plyr">Plyr</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="http://paypal.github.io/accessible-html5-video-player/">
              Paypal accessible media player
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>
